  "behavior": [
    "CanonicalClient now has dedicated refresh_credential and cancellation-aware refresh_credential_with_cancel methods, while generic command paths continue to refuse auth.*. Callers supply their successor bearer and explicitly provision its current key/device/credential binding; no credential issuance, implicit enrollment or fallback is added.",
    "The same physical signed peer verifies correlated auth.session, original Identity, connect/2, unchanged identified assurance, future expiry and a new bounded opaque token before installing state. Returned CanonicalAuthentication exposes no token/credential. Current usable expiry is bounded by the pinned server key; the prior incarnation bounds the entire refresh exchange.",
    "Controlled signed peers exercise foreign owner/profile/assurance, expired/empty/unchanged tokens, wrong reply correlation, missing and streaming replies, explicit signed refusal, cancellation and invalid input. Bad or uncertain exchanges retire the physical peer without installing candidate state; explicit correlated refusal preserves the previous local state and sanitizes backend text.",
    "The actual Connect listener/public SDK positive case runs both EdDSA and ES256. A seven-second predecessor is replaced with a separately issued/bound history-only successor. New conversation creation is refused, history still succeeds after actual predecessor expiry and keepalive works with the new opaque token. This proves real listener/Store authority, client expiry update and effective attenuation, not only upstream peer unit behavior.",
    "The second actual listener case rejects a valid same-owner successor lacking an explicit signing-key binding and rejects a different owner. The original gate still creates a Conversation and acknowledges its old keepalive afterwards. No test-only protocol driver is installed in these runtime cases."
  ],
